{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>See, I have placed before you, etc.</b> Its saying at the outset <b>see</b> in singular and concluding by saying in plural is because in the category of seeing they are all equal as one person, and there is no differentiation among them; but in the matter of what they are, not all of them are equal in category. Therefore it says ״לִפְנֵיכֶם״ (before you, plural), and likewise everything it says afterward in the verse in plural — ״come and possess,״ etc. — is not in the category of equality as one." "<b>Come and possess the land, etc.</b> The reason it was necessary to repeat the mention of <b>the land</b> and did not say 'it' — though it is understood that it refers back to the land mentioned nearby — is that the land mentioned nearby, which they saw that HaShem had given, is the land of Sihon and Og, which He gave to the children of Gad and the children of Reuben. Therefore, when it said ״come and possess,״ it was necessary to specify what they would possess, and it said <b>the land which HaShem swore</b>, etc. — meaning, for the land that the children of Gad and the children of Reuben took was not included in the oath, as I wrote in parashat Matot (Numbers 32:7), and we proved it from Sifrei."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:14.746975162Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}